nrc-cyber-rg-5-71 pack: content licence
=======================================

This pack is derived from two sources:

    NRC Regulatory Guide 5.71, Cyber Security Programs for Nuclear Power
    Reactors, Rev. 1, February 2023
    Publisher: U.S. Nuclear Regulatory Commission. Accession ML22258A204

    10 CFR Part 73, section 73.54, Protection of digital computer and
    communication systems and networks (eCFR public text; eCFR pin-check
    2026-11-09; section unchanged since 2017-01-01)

Source licence: Public Domain (US Government work, 17 U.S.C. 105) (tier 1;
see ../../docs/SOURCE-VETTING.md). No source-material download link is published.

The sources are works of the United States Government and are not subject to
copyright protection in the United States (17 U.S.C. 105). Anyone may
reproduce, transform, and redistribute the guide and regulation text for any
purpose, including commercially, without permission and without any
attribution or share-alike obligation.

Attribution to the NRC is courtesy (see the repository NOTICE), not a legal
obligation. The NRC does not endorse this pack or its authors.

Reconstruction: pack content is synthesized orientation notes from RG 5.71
Rev. 1 pinned facts (P9 listing-page pin, 2026-11-08), 10 CFR 73.54 public
eCFR slices, and carried nrc-nuclear SDOE-fence facts. Verbatim from eCFR
text is capped at two sentences by licence policy and RG 5.71-derived notes
are synthesized; this pack contains zero quotations. G-02 and G-03 are named
only as idea-stage neighbours, and their text is never reproduced here. No
security-control implementation guidance and no threat-actor or tactic
detail appear in this pack.

NOTE: this file governs the CONTENT of this pack. Repository tooling stays
MIT and does not govern pack content (see ../../LICENSE).
